  "followUpGuide": [
    "TTL eviction needs an injected clock and purge on reads and writes. Decide how late events for an evicted ID behave: removing the finalized marker would let them recreate the message. Keep a bounded tombstone or require fresh IDs when completed text is discarded.",
    "",
    "Offsets help detect duplicate or out-of-order deltas.",
    "",
    "Finish reason is metadata stored next to completed text during finalization."
  ],
  "complexityAnalysis": [
    "- Let C be retained characters, D retained delta parts (including empty strings), and M message IDs. Joining one buffer costs O(characters + parts), so empty deltas still contribute time and memory.",
    "- Concatenate strings naively: repeated immutable-string copies can cost O(C^2) for one message receiving one-character deltas. Time also includes event processing. Space: O(C + M).",
    "- List buffers without a completed-text cache: Time: O(1) amortized per append, O(characters + parts) per get or finalization. Repeated reads can cost quadratic work as the buffer grows. Space: O(C + D + M).",
    "- Shipped completed-text cache: Time: O(characters + parts) for first finalization, O(1) for later finalized reads and repeated final events, and O(characters + parts) for an unfinished get. Space: O(C + D + M); cached strings can duplicate retained characters by a constant factor."
  ],
  "solutionGuide": [
    "Keep buffers by ID and a finalized set. Join once on finalization and cache that result; later final events and reads return the cached string. Ignore new deltas after finalization.",
    "",
    "```python",
    "class TokenAssembler:",
    "    def __init__(self):",
    "        self.parts = {}",
    "        self.finalized = set()",
    "        self.completed = {}",
    "",
    "    def apply(self, event: dict):",
    "        message_id = event[\"id\"]",
    "        if message_id in self.finalized:",
    "            return self.completed[message_id] if event.get(\"final\") else None",
    "        if message_id not in self.parts:",
    "            self.parts[message_id] = []",
    "        if \"delta\" in event:",
    "            self.parts[message_id].append(event[\"delta\"])",
    "        if event.get(\"final\"):",
    "            self.finalized.add(message_id)",
    "            self.completed[message_id] = \"\".join(self.parts[message_id])",
    "            return self.completed[message_id]",
    "        return None",
    "",
    "    def get(self, message_id):",
    "        if message_id in self.finalized:",
    "            return self.completed[message_id]",
    "        if message_id not in self.parts:",
    "            return None",
    "        return \"\".join(self.parts[message_id])",
    "```"
  ]
